  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance d&#x2019;urgence aux retourn&#xe9;s tchadiens du Soudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide protection, shelter and essential household item, and water, sanitation and hygiene assistance to returnees in Ouaddai and Sila. This IOM project distributes US$325,000 through cash and voucher assistance, distributes shelter kits, facilitates access to safe drinking water, and provides essential protection services including registrations and referrals. The shelter and essential household item component of the project provides humanitarian assistance to 20,800 people, including 3,100 persons with disabilities. The protection component provides humanitarian assistance to 18,100 people, including 2,700 persons with disabilities. The water, sanitation and hygiene component provides humanitarian assistance to 10,400 people, including 1,600 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
